## Setup

Install [Homebrew](https://brew.sh), then run in the repository:

```sh
brew bundle
mise install                          # tools from mise.toml and mise.lock, about 1.2 GB once
git config core.hooksPath .githooks
scripts/check
gh extension install github/gh-stack  # optional: stacked PRs
```

Homebrew installs mise and the GitHub CLI. mise installs every build tool at the version in
`mise.toml`: clang {{llvm_version}} with clang-tidy, clangd and clang-format, CMake {{cmake_version}} and
Ninja {{ninja_version}}. `mise.lock` pins each download by checksum. Use mise {{mise_version}} or newer.
`mise install` asks you to trust `mise.toml` once. `scripts/check` starts itself inside
`mise exec`, so it works in any shell. The git hook runs the checks before each push.

Linux works the same way without Homebrew: install mise and the GitHub CLI, then run the same
commands.

Editor: point clangd at the pinned one (`mise which clangd`), not Xcode's. `.clangd` points it at
the compile commands that `scripts/check` writes to `build/dev/`.

## Commands

```sh
scripts/check                                      # every quality gate: format, lint, build, test
scripts/format                                     # format the C++ files
mise exec --locked -- cmake --build --preset dev   # build
mise exec --locked -- ctest --preset dev           # run the tests
build/dev/{{package}}                              # run the program
```

The `dev` preset builds with sanitizers for checking, not for release.

`scripts/check` is the single list of gates. The git hook and CI run it too.

AI agents follow [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Reviews apply [CODING_STANDARDS.md](CODING_STANDARDS.md).
